---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { siteData } from "../data/portfolio";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title={`About | ${siteData.name}`}
	description="About Yalçıncan Ulus, his approach to building products, and what he enjoys working on."
>
	<Header resumePath={siteData.resumePath} />

	<main class="about">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="about__body">
				<h1 class="about__title"><span class="mark">#</span> about</h1>
				<p class="about__lead">
					&gt; I am a full-stack engineer based in Türkiye, specializing in the broader TypeScript ecosystem.
				</p>

				<p>
					Although my bachelor's and master's degrees are in a different engineering field, I have always written software. For my master's thesis at Istanbul Technical University (İTÜ), I built my own custom software and used it for all of my research. With my thesis advisor, I co-authored and published a <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/buildings13040915" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">research paper</a>. All of the analyses and simulations in that paper were done with my software. It has been cited 20+ times so far and continues to be cited regularly.
				</p>

				<p>
					To move into software engineering professionally, I completed the full-stack curriculum of <a href="https://www.theodinproject.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Odin Project</a>, an open-source curriculum written and maintained by industry professionals.
				</p>

				<p>
					Since then, I have built and deployed many real-world, working applications. I use proven, industry-standard technologies as well as newer ones, and I like to follow the cutting edge of the TypeScript ecosystem. In my selected projects, you can see traditional tools like Node.js and Express alongside Bun, Elysia and the TanStack libraries.
				</p>

				<p>
					LLMs are changing software development rapidly. They are extremely useful and save a lot of time, and almost every company now uses AI in some form. I follow developer tooling and AI as closely as I follow web development, and I have used AI to different degrees in my projects. I can work with as much or as little AI as a task calls for. I built a working <a href="https://github.com/yalcincanulus/social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">social media platform</a>, the final project of The Odin Project, <strong>without AI</strong>. I used it occasionally in my <a href="https://github.com/yalcincanulus/price-tracking-app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">price tracker</a> project. For my document sharing platform, <a href="https://github.com/yalcincanulus/bitig-flow" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bitig Flow</a>, I fully leveraged LLMs, while I made the architectural decisions and reviewed all of the code myself. Using AI well is a skill in itself, and it lets me do more in less time.
				</p>

				<p>
					I use AI to move faster, not to do my thinking for me. If that is the kind of engineer you are looking for, I would love to hear from you.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer
		email={siteData.email}
		githubUrl={siteData.githubUrl}
		linkedinUrl={siteData.linkedinUrl}
		resumePath={siteData.resumePath}
		name={siteData.name}
	/>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about {
		padding-block: 6rem 4rem;
	}

	.about__body {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	.about__title {
		font-size: 1.75rem;
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.about__body p {
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	.about__body .about__lead {
		color: var(--text);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.about__body a {
		color: var(--accent);
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
	}

	.about__body a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.about__body strong {
		color: var(--text);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.about {
			padding-top: 4rem;
		}
	}
</style>
